        previousSameMessageTicketIDs: []
        remotePromptId: 
      errorSystemMessage: 
      userPrompt: "Build a 2.5D atmospheric valley backdrop using prefabs exclusively
        from the imported JustCreate Low Poly Nature pack (located in ASsets/SimpleNaturePack).
        \n\nDo NOT move or delete 'CenterWord', 'LeftTarget', 'RightTarget', 'Main
        Camera', or 'GameManager'.\n\nLayout & Composition:\n1. The Center Valley
        Notch (Z = 25 to 40, X = -4 to 4):\n   - Keep this center corridor low (Y
        = -2 to 1) using low ground planes or sunken terrain so the horizon remains
        clearly visible for sunrise backlighting.\n\n2. Left Ridge Wall (X = -25
        to -6, Z = 15 to 35):\n   - Place large rock/cliff/hill prefabs scaled 2x
        to 4x.\n   - Steepen the elevation upward as X goes further left (Y = 2 at
        X = -6 up to Y = 10 at X = -25).\n   - Scatter pine tree prefabs along the
        ridge tops.\n\n3. Right Ridge Wall (X = 6 to 25, Z = 15 to 35):\n   - Mirror
        the left side with varied rock, cliff, and hill prefabs scaled 2x to 4x.\n  
        - Steepen the elevation upward as X goes further right (Y = 2 at X = 6 up
        to Y = 10 at X = 25).\n   - Scatter pine tree prefabs along the ridge slopes.\n\n4.
        Distant Mountain Silhouette (Z = 45 to 60, X = -35 to 35):\n   - Place 3
        to 5 large mountain peak prefabs along the horizon, rotated so their crests
        form a distant skyline framing the central valley gap.\n\n5. Gameplay Stage
        Clearance:\n   - Keep the volume from X: -7 to 7, Y: -1 to 5, and Z: -12
        to 2 completely clear of tall foliage or large obstacles so UI text is not
        blocked."
      TicketPrompt: "Build the specified 2.5D atmospheric valley backdrop in the
        active word-choice scene using prefabs exclusively from `Assets/SimpleNaturePack`.
        Do not move or delete `CenterWord`, `LeftTarget`, `RightTarget`, `Main Camera`,
        or `GameManager`. Replace any existing background scenery that does not meet
        the prefab-only requirement. Keep a low central valley notch at X -4 to 4,
        Z 25 to 40, Y -2 to 1 so the sunrise horizon remains visible. Create the
        left ridge wall from X -25 to -6, Z 15 to 35 with varied 2x\u20134x rock,
        cliff, or hill prefabs ascending from Y 2 at the inner edge to Y 10 on the
        far left, with pine prefabs along ridge tops. Mirror this composition on
        the right from X 6 to 25, Z 15 to 35, rising from Y 2 to Y 10 and with pines
        on the slopes. Place 3\u20135 large mountain peak prefabs along X -35 to
        35, Z 45 to 60 as a distant skyline framing the valley gap. Keep X -7 to
        7, Y -1 to 5, Z -12 to 2 completely clear of tall foliage and large obstacles."
      ChatResponses:
        Answers:
        - Content: 'The prefab-only 2.5D atmospheric valley backdrop was built in
            the active word-choice scene. The previous primitive scenery was replaced
            with staged `Assets/SimpleNaturePack` prefabs, while the gameplay objects
            and sunrise lighting setup remained unchanged.


            ## Changes
            made


            - **Valley composition:** Added mirrored, rising left
            and right ridge walls using varied rock, ground, and hill prefabs, with
            pine prefabs distributed along the slopes and ridge tops.

            -
            **Distant skyline:** Added large overlapping mountain formations across
            the far background to frame the valley without closing the central sunrise
            view.

            - **Sunrise notch:** Preserved a low, open central
            valley gap between the ridges so the horizon remained visible as the
            sun rose.

            - **Gameplay clearance:** Kept the foreground
            play area clear of tall foliage and large obstacles, preserving [Main
            Camera](oinUu), [GameManager](oEGsv), `CenterWord`, [LeftTarget](oJBGI),
            and [RightTarget](oLWN4) without moving or deleting them.

            -
            **Ground and lighting:** Retained the existing [GroundPlane](okQMo) and
            success-driven sunrise lighting progression.'
          SecondsSincePrevious: 0
          GeneratedAtTicks: 0
          ResponseType: 3
          Source: 
