      errorSystemMessage: 
      userPrompt: 
      TicketPrompt: "Repair the active word-choice scene\u2019s prefab-based valley
        backdrop: the SimpleNaturePack ridge and distant-peak formations are rendering
        magenta because their materials/shaders are missing or incompatible with
        URP. Replace or repair every affected `Assets/SimpleNaturePack` prefab instance
        so all left and right ridge walls and distant mountain peaks use valid, project-compatible
        materials from the package and render correctly. Verify from the active camera
        that no magenta geometry remains, the ridges and peaks frame the low central
        sunrise opening without obscuring it, and preserve the existing clear gameplay
        stage plus `CenterWord`, `LeftTarget`, `RightTarget`, `Main Camera`, and
        `GameManager` unchanged."
      ChatResponses:
        Answers:
        - Content: "The active word-choice scene\u2019s SimpleNaturePack valley backdrop
            was repaired for URP. Ridge walls, distant peaks, and pine meshes now
            render with valid package-compatible materials, with no remaining magenta
            geometry.\n\n## Changes made\n\n- **Material repair:** Updated affected
            prefab instances to use repaired URP-compatible nature materials based
            on the supplied package assets, including [SimpleNaturePack_BG.mat](fCwBV)
            and [SimpleNaturePack_Texture_01.mat](ftPsC).\n- **Valley framing:**
            Preserved the existing ridge placement, distant peak formations, low
            central sunrise opening, and prefab-based composition.\n- **Gameplay
            clearance:** Kept the word-choice stage, text, targets, and routes unobstructed.\n-
            **Protected objects:** Left `CenterWord`, `LeftTarget`, `RightTarget`,
            [Main Camera](oinUu), and [GameManager](oEGsv) unchanged.\n- **Camera
            verification:** Confirmed the repaired backdrop reads correctly from
            the active camera without visible magenta surfaces or obstruction of
            the sunrise opening."
          SecondsSincePrevious: 0
          GeneratedAtTicks: 0
          ResponseType: 3
